{
 "@context": {
  "fylite": "urn:fylite:"
 },
 "@id": "fylite:CaseCatalogue/app",
 "@type": "fylite:CaseCatalogue/1",
 "fylite:note": "The worked cases a published page offers from a menu. ★★A case is a SESSION DOCUMENT -- byte-for-byte the shape `导出 → 会话文件` writes -- and applying one goes through the same `FySession.apply` an imported file goes through. So a reader can save their own run and it is a case; and a case cannot drift into a format only the menu can read. What a case may NOT do is carry a result: it is a set of INPUTS, and the page still has to run.  ★★`fylite:bar` NAMES THE BAR, and since 2026-08-24 it is honoured: the menu machinery is `scenario.js`'s (`S.cases`), not one bar's private code, so any bar that carries a `<select id=\"<page>-<bar>-case\">` gets the cases written for it.  ★`fylite:initial` marks the one case a bar starts a FIRST VISIT on (no trace of the reader in `localStorage`).  It is NOT the factory settings — the 「缺省」 case is still the one step back to those, and it stays in the menu.  A case is never applied over a session the reader already has.",
 "fylite:cases": [
  {
